---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Pavan Raheja — Quant Lab"
  description="An AI-native trading desk, run in the open. Live multi-venue track record, every thesis explainable, every loss published."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-xs font-medium text-brand-600 uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Quant Lab</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">An AI-native trading desk, run in the open.</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
        Live multi-venue track record, every thesis explainable, every loss published.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Thesis -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">Why now</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        In Spring 2026, YC's Garry Tan published a Request for Startups titled <em>"AI-Native Hedge Funds"</em> &mdash; <em>"not a research assistant&hellip; an AI-driven investment engine"</em> with specialized agents for statistical arbitrage, regime-based backtests, liquidity-aware sizing, and <strong>mandatory per-trade explainability</strong>.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        a16z's State of Crypto 2025 shows prediction-market volume up ~5x in a year and Hyperliquid clearing &gt;$1B annualized revenue &mdash; and a16z itself now holds ~$356M of HYPE, its largest external token position.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
        I've been operating at that intersection since before it was a thesis. Quant Lab is the public, auditable version of what those funded teams build behind closed doors.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- What you get -->
    <div class="mb-12 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100">
      <p class="text-xs font-medium text-brand-600 uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">What you get</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Every pick ships as a <strong>structured object</strong>, not a chat message:
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs font-mono text-gray-600 bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        market &middot; venue &middot; side &middot; entry &middot; size% &middot; thesis &middot; confidence &middot; invalidation &middot; exit
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-2">
        {[
          ['Evidence chain', 'the signals that fired'],
          ['Confidence weighting', 'sized for a typical retail account, capacity-warned'],
          ['Competing thesis', 'the bear case, stated'],
          ['Invalidation criteria', 'the exact condition that kills the trade'],
          ['Live status', 'open / won / lost &mdash; updated, never deleted'],
        ].map(([label, body]) => (
          <div class="flex gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500">
            <span class="text-brand-400 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">&rarr;</span>
            <span><strong class="text-gray-900 font-medium">{label}</strong> &mdash; <span set:html={body} /></span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- The moat -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">The moat: radical transparency</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
        No competitor publishes their losses. Quant Lab's headline feature is a <strong>public, append-only failure log</strong> &mdash; the strategies I killed and why. Verifiable against a live multi-venue trading record and on-chain PnL. Methodology compounds; picks decay. The track record is the asset.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Where it sits -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">Where it sits in the market</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
        The funded layer (Kairos, Valence, Glider) sells <em>execution</em> &mdash; speed, unified order routing, on-chain automation. <strong>None sell edge.</strong> Quant Lab is the research/edge layer that feeds those rails: picks route into prediction-market terminals via open Builder Codes, so subscribers act on a pick in one click. I supply the alpha; they absorb execution and regulatory burden.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Pricing -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Pricing &mdash; launching</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        {[
          { tier: 'Free', price: '$0', what: '1 delayed pick per week &middot; full public failure log &middot; the proof engine' },
          { tier: 'Research', price: '~$49&ndash;79/mo', what: 'Real-time picks &middot; full reasoning &middot; open-position dashboard' },
          { tier: 'Pro', price: '~$199/mo', what: 'Above &middot; methodology deep-dives &middot; raw pick API/webhook feed &middot; vault read-through' },
        ].map((row) => (
          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline gap-2 sm:gap-6">
            <div class="sm:w-28 flex-shrink-0">
              <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">{row.tier}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-brand-600 font-mono">{row.price}</p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed" set:html={row.what} />
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-4">
        Flat subscription &middot; no performance fee at the research layer. Selling research, not managing money &mdash; clean regulatory line, lower trust friction.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- One-line proof -->
    <div class="mb-12 p-6 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-brand-500 bg-brand-50">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed italic">
        "I operate the AI-native, multi-venue, fully-transparent trading desk that YC just wrote a Request for Startups about and a16z is putting $356M behind &mdash; and I publish my losses."
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Get notified at launch</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        The free tier and failure log open first. Subscribe for launch updates and the first delayed picks.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/newsletter"
        class="inline-block px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg bg-brand-600 text-white text-sm font-medium hover:bg-brand-700 transition-colors"
      >
        Get launch updates &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- About the author -->
    <div class="pt-10 border-t border-gray-100">
      <p class="text-xs font-medium text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wide mb-4">About the operator</p>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <img src="/pavan.jpg" alt="Pavan Raheja" class="w-14 h-14 rounded-xl object-cover object-top flex-shrink-0" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm mb-1">Pavan Raheja</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
            AI Product Manager, crypto investor, and operator based in Dubai. Runs live systematic trading strategies across prediction markets, Hyperliquid perps, and Binance futures &mdash; with documented PnL, automated guardrails, and a published failure log.
          </p>
          <a href="/work" class="text-xs text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 mt-2 inline-block">See full background &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </section>
</Layout>
